# - internal/collections, internal/bodyprocessors, internal/cookies,
#   internal/url, internal/corazawaf and http: collections were Go maps, so
#   ARGS, cookies, headers and their _NAMES came out in a new order on every
#   evaluation, and a chain reading its parent's last match (TX:0-9,
#   MATCHED_VAR) could deny a request on one transaction and pass it on the
#   next (CRS 942130, 942131, 942521). A Map keeps its keys in insertion
#   order, and the parsers add in input order. coraza-caddy feeds headers
#   itself, from a map, so header order under it is still unsorted.
#   Upstream: issue #1815 and PR #1834 (2026-10-26), open at 08aa511.
